8 implied vol is about 23.5–25.5%, with 24.0% at the money. Realized vol is 29–31% across 3-month, 6-month and 1-year windows. That is a discount of roughly 5–7 vol points. Skew is nearly flat, so upside strikes aren't expensive.\n- **The earnings case holds.** Consensus 2027 EPS growth is 14%, and estimates are up 3% over the past quarter. A 4% multiple de-rating would still leave roughly 9–10% price upside through 2027, if the 14% is delivered.\n\n**Against adding**\n- **Rate path.** Futures price about 50bp of CMA cuts, taking the policy rate from 4.50% to 4.00%. Governor Ashby's base case is one 25bp cut in 2027, and she said markets \"may be getting ahead of themselves.\" The factsheet says 50bp lower rates have lifted the basket P/E by about 1.5 points. So the 25bp gap is worth about 0.75 points, or roughly 4% of the 19x forward P/E. That is a mild drag, not a thesis-breaker.\n- **Concentration.** Voltaris and Tarnwell are 25% of the fund, so the earnings case rests on two names.\n- **Little cushion.** 19x is already a growth multiple. If backlog conversion slips and the CMA stays hawkish, both risks hit together.\n\n**Not checked**\n- Whether the 19x already embeds the market-implied rate path.\n- The 19x against its historical range.\n- The call premium against the roughly 4% policy cushion. Do this before sizing.\n- Realized vol is backward-looking, and implied vol can sit below it for good reasons.\n\nThe detail is in n2.r1 (valuation) and n3.r1 (option pricing).","ttft_ms":4895,"type":"result","duration_ms":39567,"uuid":"d8191902-24b9-43e4-a184-207f072dba30","ttft_stream_ms":3887,"time_to_request_ms":128,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":8,"system_prompt":10,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":8,"input_attachments":33,"input_hooks":8,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":6,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":16,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":7,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":6